§ `ss 2, 3, 6, 7 -- is my payment apportionable`

#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `the same rent under an oral tenancy`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `monthly salary, employee dies 11 Mar`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `monthly pension, pensioner dies 16 Apr`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `dividend for 2025, shareholder dies 2 Jul`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `dividend for leap year 2024, shareholder dies 1 Mar`
#ASSERT `Is my payment apportionable` `half-yearly trust income, beneficiary dies 1 Apr`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my payment apportionable` `a so-called dividend that returns capital`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my payment apportionable` `an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my payment apportionable` `rent with a no-apportionment clause`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my payment apportionable` `a one-off fee`

#ASSERT `What does the Act do with my payment` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` EQUALS `it accrues from day to day under section 3`
#ASSERT `What does the Act do with my payment` `a so-called dividend that returns capital` EQUALS `a return or reimbursement of capital, which section 2 takes out of "dividends"`
#ASSERT `What does the Act do with my payment` `an annual sum under a policy of assurance` EQUALS `excluded by section 6 as an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
#ASSERT `What does the Act do with my payment` `rent with a no-apportionment clause` EQUALS `excluded by section 7 by express stipulation`
#ASSERT `What does the Act do with my payment` `a one-off fee` EQUALS `not periodical income, so outside section 3`

§ `ss 3, 5(1) -- how much has accrued to me`

#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` EQUALS (JUST 3100)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `the same rent under an oral tenancy` EQUALS (JUST 3100)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar` EQUALS (JUST 5900)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `monthly salary, employee dies 11 Mar` EQUALS (JUST 2000)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `monthly pension, pensioner dies 16 Apr` EQUALS (JUST 1500)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `dividend for 2025, shareholder dies 2 Jul` EQUALS (JUST 18200)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `dividend for leap year 2024, shareholder dies 1 Mar` EQUALS (JUST 6000)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `half-yearly trust income, beneficiary dies 1 Apr` EQUALS (JUST 9000)
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `a so-called dividend that returns capital` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `an annual sum under a policy of assurance` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `rent, interest ended the day the quarter began` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What part of the payment had accrued to me` `rent, interest ended the day the rent fell due` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What can I recover after just allowances` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` EQUALS (JUST 2790)
#ASSERT `What can I recover after just allowances` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar` EQUALS (JUST 5900)

§ `s 4 -- when is my share payable`

#ASSERT `Which limb of section 4 fixes when I am paid` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` EQUALS `section 4(a): when the entire portion becomes due`
#ASSERT `Which limb of section 4 fixes when I am paid` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar` EQUALS `section 4(b): when the next entire portion would have been payable`

#ASSERT `When can I recover my share` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` EQUALS (JUST (Date 1 4 2025))
#ASSERT `When can I recover my share` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar` EQUALS (JUST (Date 1 4 2025))
#ASSERT `When can I recover my share` `dividend for 2025, shareholder dies 2 Jul` EQUALS (JUST (Date 1 3 2026))
#ASSERT `When can I recover my share` `rent with a no-apportionment clause` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT NOT `Can I recover my share on` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` (Date 1 3 2025)
#ASSERT `Can I recover my share on` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` (Date 1 4 2025)
#ASSERT NOT `Can I recover my share on` `dividend for 2025, shareholder dies 2 Jul` (Date 1 1 2026)

§ `s 5 -- who may recover, from whom, and how`

#ASSERT `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `the person whose interest ended`
#ASSERT `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `that person's executor or administrator`
#ASSERT `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `that person's assign`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `someone with no interest in the payment`

#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` `that person's executor or administrator` EQUALS `by suit against whoever receives the entire rent, not from the tenant or the land`
#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `quarterly rent on land, lease ended by re-entry 1 Mar` `the person whose interest ended` EQUALS `by suit against whoever receives the entire rent, not from the tenant or the land`
#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `monthly salary, employee dies 11 Mar` `that person's executor or administrator` EQUALS `from the payer, with the same remedies as for the entire portion`
#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `dividend for 2025, shareholder dies 2 Jul` `that person's assign` EQUALS `from the payer, with the same remedies as for the entire portion`
#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb` `someone with no interest in the payment` EQUALS `the Act gives me no remedy`
#ASSERT `How do I recover my share` `a so-called dividend that returns capital` `the person whose interest ended` EQUALS `the Act gives me no remedy`

#ASSERT NOT `May I go to the payer directly for my share` `quarterly rent on land, life-tenant landlord dies 1 Feb`
#ASSERT `May I go to the payer directly for my share` `monthly salary, employee dies 11 Mar`

